# Provenance and publication

Before publishing an app or component, record:

- The behavior implemented and its acceptance tests.
- References used, with exact URLs, versions, and dates.
- The authorization basis for any analysis target.
- Whether any code or assets were copied; if so, the applicable license and notices.
- Implementation authorship, limitations, and test results.

Keep target binaries, private captures, credentials, paid assets, and private documents out of this repository. Do not commit decompiled proprietary code. Write independent implementations from permitted behavioral observations and public specifications. When rights or terms remain unclear, pause that analysis or publication and use an authorized/open-source target instead.

Review Git history as well as current files before making a private repository public. Deleting a sensitive file in a later commit does not remove it from earlier commits.
